      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f4cf86698ffeUxivaGxP3PJdIA\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed the research. Here is the detailed report.\n\n---\n\n# A2E Suite / Twenty server — conventions for adding a domain module (for a `chat` module)\n\n## 0. Critical framing: there are TWO entity systems in this repo\n\nThis is Twenty 2.39 (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/upgrade/constants/twenty-current-version.constant.ts`). Before writing any code, understand that the repo has two distinct persistence patterns, and your `chat` module must pick one per table:\n\n| | CRM/product objects (\"standard objects\") | Platform/instance tables |\n|---|---|---|\n| Definition | plain class in `src/modules/<domain>/standard-objects/*.workspace-entity.ts` extending `BaseWorkspaceEntity` | TypeORM class with `@Entity`, `@Column`, etc. under `src/engine/core-modules/**` or `src/engine/metadata-modules/**` |\n| Storage | **per-workspace Postgres schema** (`getWorkspaceSchemaName(workspaceId)`) | single `core` schema, rows carry `workspaceId` |\n| Registration | metadata DB rows provisioned from `twenty-shared` catalog + server builders | TypeORM glob auto-load (`core.datasource.ts`) + `TypeOrmModule.forFeature` in the module |\n| GraphQL CRUD | auto-generated from metadata (`WorkspaceSchemaFactory`) | hand-written resolvers |\n| Scoping | workspace schema + permissions in `WorkspaceRepository` (no `workspaceId` column) | explicit `workspaceId` column + `WorkspaceScopedRepository` (or `WorkspaceRelatedEntity` base) |\n| Soft delete | `deletedAt` field metadata; `WorkspaceRepository.softDelete/restore` | `@DeleteDateColumn` or a `deletedAt timestamptz` column |\n\n`note`/`task`/`company`/`person` are **standard objects** — they have no `@Entity`/`@Column`/`@Resolver`. A `chat` product object should be defined via the app SDK / standard-object catalog, while a server-domain module holds behavior (services, resolvers, query hooks, realtime).\n\nThe repo's own guidance codifies this: `docs/plan/04-twenty-native-law.md` §0 and §3 (`server domain-modules → module behavior (chat service, accounting jobs)`; \"Hand-written TypeORM entity unless server logic demands it (then domain module + upgrade command)\"). Also `docs/plan/03-integration-blueprint.md` §4 defines the realtime `chat` topic.\n\n---\n\n## 1. `src/modules/modules.module.ts` — registration\n\nFile: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/modules.module.ts` (22 lines)\n\n```ts\n@Module({\n  imports: [\n    MessagingModule,\n    CalendarModule,\n    ConnectedAccountModule,\n    OnboardingInviteSuggestionsModule,\n    WorkflowModule,\n    WorkspaceMemberModule,\n  ],\n  providers: [],\n  exports: [],\n})\nexport class ModulesModule {}\n```\n\n`ModulesModule` is imported by `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/app.module.ts` (line 66).\n\n**But** domain modules that contribute **GraphQL resolvers** are registered differently — in `CoreEngineModule`:\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/core-engine.module.ts` imports e.g. `SendEmailModule` (line 86/143), `CreateCalendarEventModule` (83/144), `CallRecordingModule` (84/145), `DashboardModule` (85/183), `EmailingModule` (35/125), `MessagingWebhooksModule`, `ChannelSyncModule`.\n\nWhy it matters: resolvers are discovered by scope. In `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-config/graphql-config.service.ts`:\n\n```ts\nconst config: YogaDriverConfig = {\n  autoSchemaFile: true,\n  include: [CoreEngineModule],\n  resolverSchemaScope: 'core',\n  ...\n};\n```\n\n`ResolversExplorerService` (node_modules/@nestjs/graphql) walks the `include` module's transitive imports and keeps only resolvers whose metadata scope matches. There are three decorators:\n\n- `@CoreResolver()` → `resolver-schema-scope 'core'` → `POST /graphql` (`src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-config/decorators/core-resolver.decorator.ts`)\n- `@MetadataResolver()` → `'metadata'` → `POST /metadata` (`.../metadata-resolver.decorator.ts`)\n- `@AdminResolver()` → `'admin'` (`.../admin-resolver.decorator.ts`)\n\nThe metadata endpoint's `include: [MetadataGraphQLApiModule]` transitively reaches `CoreEngineModule` (`metadata-graphql-api.module.ts` → `GraphQLConfigModule` → `CoreEngineModule`), which is how domain-module `@MetadataResolver`s get onto `/metadata`.\n\n**Every resolver under `src/modules/**` is `@MetadataResolver`** (verified: calendar, call-recording, channel-sync, dashboard, emailing, send-email). So:\n\n- Behavior-only domain module → add to `ModulesModule` (or be spawned by an existing one).\n- Domain module exposing a GraphQL resolver → add its module to `CoreEngineModule.imports`, and mark the resolver `@MetadataResolver`.\n- Query hooks → registered in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/graphql/workspace-query-runner/workspace-query-hook/workspace-query-hook.module.ts` (imports `NoteQueryHookModule`, `TaskQueryHookModule`, …). Add a `ChatQueryHookModule` there.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Simplest domain module: `note` — full tree and contents\n\nFull tree (`find`):\n```\npackages/twenty-server/src/modules/note/\n  query-hooks/\n    note-delete-many.post-query.hook.ts\n    note-delete-one.post-query.hook.ts\n    note-post-query-hook.service.ts\n    note-query-hook.module.ts\n    note-restore-many.post-query.hook.ts\n    note-restore-one.post-query.hook.ts\n  standard-objects/\n    note-target.workspace-entity.ts\n    note.workspace-entity.ts\n```\n(No `<name>.module.ts`, resolver, or service: those live in the shared `WorkspaceQueryHookModule` and in the metadata engine.)\n\n### 2a. The standard-object workspace entity (no decorators)\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/note/standard-objects/note.workspace-entity.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { type ActorMetadata, type RichTextMetadata } from 'twenty-shared/types';\n\nimport { BaseWorkspaceEntity } from 'src/engine/twenty-orm/base.workspace-entity';\nimport { type EntityRelation } from 'src/engine/workspace-manager/workspace-migration/types/entity-relation.interface';\nimport { type AttachmentWorkspaceEntity } from 'src/modules/attachment/standard-objects/attachment.workspace-entity';\nimport { type NoteTargetWorkspaceEntity } from 'src/modules/note/standard-objects/note-target.workspace-entity';\nimport { type TimelineActivityWorkspaceEntity } from 'src/modules/timeline/standard-objects/timeline-activity.workspace-entity';\n\nexport class NoteWorkspaceEntity extends BaseWorkspaceEntity {\n  position: number;\n  title: string;\n  bodyV2: RichTextMetadata | null;\n  createdBy: ActorMetadata;\n  updatedBy: ActorMetadata;\n  noteTargets: EntityRelation<NoteTargetWorkspaceEntity[]>;\n  attachments: EntityRelation<AttachmentWorkspaceEntity[]>;\n  timelineActivities: EntityRelation<TimelineActivityWorkspaceEntity[]>;\n  searchVector: string;\n}\n```\n\n`note-target.workspace-entity.ts` shows polymorphic relations:\n```ts\nexport class NoteTargetWorkspaceEntity extends BaseWorkspaceEntity {\n  note: EntityRelation<NoteWorkspaceEntity> | null;\n  noteId: string | null;\n  targetPerson: EntityRelation<PersonWorkspaceEntity> | null;\n  targetPersonId: string | null;\n  ...\n  custom: EntityRelation<CustomWorkspaceEntity>;\n}\n```\n\nNote there are **no `@ObjectType`, `@Entity`, `@Column`, `@Field`, no `id`, no `workspaceId`, no `createdAt/deletedAt`** on the class — those come from `BaseWorkspaceEntity` and from field metadata.\n\nThe **field-level metadata** (id, createdAt, updatedAt, deletedAt, title, bodyV2, searchVector, relations) is declared server-side in:\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-note-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`\n\nRepresentative excerpt (system fields + a normal field + relation):\n```ts\nexport const buildNoteStandardFlatFieldMetadatas = ({ ... }) => ({\n  id: createStandardFieldFlatMetadata({\n    objectName, workspaceId,\n    context: {\n      fieldName: 'id',\n      type: FieldMetadataType.UUID,\n      label: i18nLabel(msg({ message: `Id`, context: 'fieldMetadata.label' })),\n      icon: 'Icon123',\n      isSystem: true, isNullable: false, isUIEditable: false,\n      defaultValue: 'uuid',\n    }, ...\n  }),\n  deletedAt: createStandardFieldFlatMetadata({\n    context: {\n      fieldName: 'deletedAt',\n      type: FieldMetadataType.DATE_TIME,\n      isSystem: true, isNullable: true, isUIEditable: false,\n      settings: { displayFormat: DateDisplayFormat.RELATIVE },\n    }, ...\n  }),\n  bodyV2: createStandardFieldFlatMetadata({\n    context: { fieldName: 'bodyV2', type: FieldMetadataType.RICH_TEXT, ... }\n  }),\n  noteTargets: createStandardRelationFieldFlatMetadata({\n    context: {\n      type: FieldMetadataType.RELATION, fieldName: 'noteTargets',\n      targetObjectName: 'noteTarget', targetFieldName: 'note',\n      settings: { relationType: RelationType.ONE_TO_MANY },\n      ...\n    }, ...\n  }),\n});\n```\n\nThe **object-level metadata** (nameSingular/namePlural/labels/icon/searchable/shortcut) is in:\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/object-metadata/create-standard-flat-object-metadata.util.ts`:\n```ts\nnote: ({ now, workspaceId, ... }) =>\n  createStandardObjectFlatMetadata({\n    objectName: 'note',\n    context: {\n      universalIdentifier: STANDARD_OBJECTS.note.universalIdentifier,\n      nameSingular: 'note',\n      namePlural: 'notes',\n      labelSingular: i18nLabel(msg({ message: `Note`, context: 'objectMetadata.labelSingular' })),\n      labelPlural: i18nLabel(msg({ message: `Notes`, context: 'objectMetadata.labelPlural' })),\n      icon: 'IconNotes',\n      isSearchable: true,\n      shortcut: 'N',\n      labelIdentifierFieldMetadataName: 'title',\n    }, ...\n  }),\n```\nThe map is aggregated by `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/object-metadata/build-standard-flat-object-metadata-maps.util.ts`.\n\nThe **cross-package single source of truth** for IDs and fields is in `twenty-shared`:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object-universal-identifiers.constant.ts` (`note: '20202020-0b00-45cd-b6f6-6cd806fc6804'`)\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object-fields.constant.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts` (`STANDARD_OBJECTS.note = { universalIdentifier, fields, indexes, views }`)\n- `AllStandardObjectName = keyof typeof STANDARD_OBJECTS` at `.../types/all-standard-object-name.type.ts`\n\nAdding a standard object therefore means editing both the shared catalog and the server builders (plus specs such as `standard-metadata-label-catalog.spec.ts`, `standard-field-writability.spec.ts`, `standard-object-readability.spec.ts`). **For chat, prefer shipping objects via the app SDK (`packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-chat`) unless the object is truly core.**\n\n### 2b. Query-hook module/service (the \"module\" for a standard object)\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/note/query-hooks/note-query-hook.module.ts`:\n```ts\n@Module({\n  providers: [\n    NotePostQueryHookService,\n    NoteDeleteManyPostQueryHook,\n    NoteDeleteOnePostQueryHook,\n    NoteRestoreManyPostQueryHook,\n    NoteRestoreOnePostQueryHook,\n  ],\n})\nexport class NoteQueryHookModule {}\n```\n\n`note-delete-one.post-query.hook.ts`:\n```ts\n@Injectable()\n@WorkspaceQueryHook({ key: `note.deleteOne`, type: WorkspaceQueryHookType.POST_HOOK })\nexport class NoteDeleteOnePostQueryHook implements WorkspacePostQueryHookInstance {\n  constructor(private readonly notePostQueryHookService: NotePostQueryHookService) {}\n  async execute(authContext, _objectName, payload: NoteWorkspaceEntity[]): Promise<void> {\n    await this.notePostQueryHookService.handleNoteTargetsDelete(authContext, payload);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`note-post-query-hook.service.ts` (shows ORM usage + soft delete/restore):\n```ts\n@Injectable()\nexport class NotePostQueryHookService {\n  constructor(private readonly workspaceOrmManager: WorkspaceOrmManager) {}\n\n  async handleNoteTargetsDelete(authContext, payload) {\n    const workspace = authContext.workspace;\n    assertIsDefinedOrThrow(workspace, WorkspaceNotFoundDefaultError);\n\n    await this.workspaceOrmManager.executeInWorkspaceContext(async () => {\n      const noteTargetRepository =\n        this.workspaceOrmManager.getRepository<NoteTargetWorkspaceEntity>('noteTarget');\n      await noteTargetRepository.softDelete({ noteId: In(payload.map((n) => n.id)) });\n    }, authContext);\n  }\n  // handleNoteTargetsRestore -> noteTargetRepository.restore(...)\n}\n```\n`WorkspaceOrmManager` is at `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/twenty-orm/workspace-orm.manager.ts` (`getRepository`, `runInWorkspaceTransaction`, `executeInWorkspaceContext`).\n\n### 2c. A real resolver + service example (for behavior beyond metadata CRUD)\n\nModule: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/messaging/message-outbound-manager/send-email.module.ts`\n```ts\n@Module({\n  imports: [FileEmailAttachmentModule, ToolModule, MessagingSendManagerModule,\n            ConnectedAccountMetadataModule, PermissionsModule],\n  providers: [SendEmailResolver],\n})\nexport class SendEmailModule {}\n```\n\nResolver: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/messaging/message-outbound-manager/resolvers/send-email.resolver.ts`\n```ts\n@MetadataResolver()\n@UsePipes(ResolverValidationPipe)\n@UseFilters(AuthGraphqlApiExceptionFilter)\n@UseGuards(\n  WorkspaceAuthGuard,\n  SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.SEND_EMAIL_TOOL),\n)\nexport class SendEmailResolver {\n  constructor(\n    private readonly connectedAccountMetadataService: ConnectedAccountMetadataService,\n    private readonly emailComposerService: EmailComposerService,\n    private readonly fileEmailAttachmentService: FileEmailAttachmentService,\n    private readonly sendEmailService: SendEmailService,\n  ) {}\n\n  @Mutation(() => SendEmailOutputDTO)\n  async sendEmail(\n    @Args('input') input: SendEmailInput,\n    @AuthWorkspace() workspace: WorkspaceEntity,\n    @AuthUserWorkspaceId() userWorkspaceId: string,\n  ): Promise<SendEmailOutputDTO> { ... }\n}\n```\n\nA very similar mutation exists at `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-creation-manager/resolvers/create-calendar-event.resolver.ts`.\n\n### 2d. Why note/task had no `*.module.ts` before\n\nThe `note` module today only needs metadata + query hooks; its GraphQL CRUD is auto-generated. Do not invent a `NoteModule` that duplicates metadata CRUD.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Workspace scoping\n\n### Standard objects (per-workspace schema) — no `workspaceId` column\nTable shape resolves `schemaName: getWorkspaceSchemaName(workspaceId)`:\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/twenty-orm/table-shape/utils/build-workspace-table-shape.util.ts` (line 121). The schema is selected via `WorkspaceDataSource` / `WorkspaceOrmManager`, which load the workspace auth context and permission maps:\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/twenty-orm/workspace-orm.manager.ts` (lines 100-143 `loadWorkspaceContext`). Permission enforcement lives in `WorkspaceRepository` (`.../repository/workspace-repository.ts`), methods `find/findOne/insert/update/delete/softDelete/restore`, with `applyWriteRowLevelPermissions` and `validateRLSPredicatesForRecords`.\n\n`WorkspaceAuthGuard` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/guards/workspace-auth.guard.ts`) only asserts `request.workspace` exists. `@AuthWorkspace()` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/decorators/auth/auth-workspace.decorator.ts`) reads it off the request:\n```ts\nexport const AuthWorkspace = createParamDecorator((options, ctx) => {\n  const request = getRequest(ctx);\n  if (!options?.allowUndefined && !request.workspace) {\n    throw new InternalServerErrorException(...);\n  }\n  return request.workspace;\n});\n```\nUsage: `@AuthWorkspace() workspace: WorkspaceEntity` (or destructured `{ id: workspaceId }`). Companion decorators: `AuthUserWorkspaceId`, `AuthWorkspaceMemberId` in the same folder.\n\n### Core-schema tables — explicit `workspaceId` enforced by `WorkspaceScopedRepository`\nBase: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/types/workspace-related-entity.ts`\n```ts\nexport abstract class WorkspaceRelatedEntity {\n  @Column({ nullable: false, type: 'uuid' })\n  workspaceId: string;\n\n  @ManyToOne('WorkspaceEntity', { onDelete: 'CASCADE' })\n  @JoinColumn({ name: 'workspaceId' })\n  workspace: Relation<WorkspaceEntity>;\n}\n```\nRepository: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/twenty-orm/workspace-scoped-repository/workspace-scoped-repository.ts`. **Every method takes `workspaceId` as first argument and merges it into the WHERE clause**:\n```ts\nfindOne(workspaceId: string, options: FindOneOptions<T>): Promise<T | null> {\n  this.assertWorkspaceId(workspaceId);\n  return this.repository.findOne({ ...options, where: this.mergeWorkspaceIdIntoWhere(workspaceId, options.where) });\n}\n```\nIt deliberately omits `save/saveMany/softRemove/recover/remove` (comment lines 181-187) because TypeORM would key only on the PK and could cross workspaces. `prependWorkspaceId` throws if you pass `workspaceId` yourself.\n\nSetup requires `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([entity])` plus:\n```ts\nprovideWorkspaceScopedRepository(AgentChatThreadEntity)\n```\nand injection:\n```ts\n@InjectWorkspaceScopedRepository(AgentChatThreadEntity)\nprivate readonly threadRepository: WorkspaceScopedRepository<AgentChatThreadEntity>,\n```\n(see `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-chat/ai-chat.module.ts` lines 47-52, 86-90).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Entity registration with TypeORM\n\n### Core (instance) tables\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/database/typeorm/core/core.datasource.ts`:\n```ts\nexport const typeORMCoreModuleOptions: TypeOrmModuleOptions = {\n  url: process.env.PG_DATABASE_URL,\n  type: 'postgres',\n  schema: 'core',\n  entities:\n    process.env.IS_BILLING_ENABLED === 'true'\n      ? [\n          `${isJest ? 'src/' : 'dist/'}engine/core-modules/**/*.entity{.ts,.js}`,\n          `${isJest ? 'src/' : 'dist/'}engine/metadata-modules/**/*.entity{.ts,.js}`,\n        ]\n      : [\n          `${isJest ? 'src/' : 'dist/'}engine/core-modules/**/!(billing-*).entity.{ts,js}`,\n          `${isJest ? 'src/' : 'dist/'}engine/metadata-modules/**/*.entity{.ts,.js}`,\n        ],\n  synchronize: false,\n  migrations: ... legacy-typeorm-migrations-do-not-add ...,\n};\n```\nWired in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/database/typeorm/typeorm.module.ts` via `TypeOrmModule.forRootAsync`.\n\n**Key consequence for chat:** the auto-load globs only cover `engine/core-modules/**` and `engine/metadata-modules/**`. There are **zero** `*.entity.ts` files under `src/modules/**` (verified). So a TypeORM entity placed at `src/modules/chat/entities/chat-message.entity.ts` would **not** be loaded by the core DataSource. Precedents:\n- `AgentChatThreadEntity` etc. live under `src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/...` and are loaded by the glob, then pulled into `AiChatModule` with `TypeOrmModule.forFeature`.\n- Domain modules such as `connected-account.module.ts` use `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([ConnectedAccountEntity, UserWorkspaceEntity])` where those entities are defined under `engine/`.\n\nThere is **no legacy TypeORM migration path anymore**: `core.datasource.ts` comment lines 60-64 says the migration system is frozen; new schema changes go through generated instance commands (`npx nx run twenty-server:database:migrate:generate --name <name> --type <fast|slow>`), auto-registered in `instance-commands.constant.ts` (see `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/docs/UPGRADE_COMMANDS.md`).\n\n### Workspace tables (metadata objects)\nNot TypeORM-decorated. Registered by metadata provisioning: the builders under `.../twenty-standard-application/...` produce flat metadata maps that are synced into each workspace. Runtime queries go through `WorkspaceOrmManager.getRepository(...)` / `WorkspaceDataSourceService`.\n\n### `TypeOrmModule.forFeature` usage\n`grep -l \"TypeOrmModule.forFeature\" src/modules` finds many (onboarding-invite-suggestions, channel-sync, calendar-common, emailing, workspace-member query-hooks, etc.). But again, all entity classes they reference live under `engine/`, not `src/modules/`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. GraphQL schema organization and `graphql:generate`\n\n- **There are no per-module `*.graphql` schema files in `twenty-server`.** The only `.graphql` files in the repo are:\n  - `packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/metadata/generated/schema.graphql`\n  - `packages/twenty-client-sdk/src/generate/__tests__/upstream-3.0.5/fixture/{,generated/}schema.graphql`\n  - `packages/twenty-utils/graphql-introspection-query.graphql`\n- The server is **code-first** (`autoSchemaFile: true` in `graphql-config.service.ts`, `metadata.module-factory.ts`, `admin-panel.module-factory.ts`). Resolver/DTO decorators (`@ObjectType`, `@Field`, `@Args`, `@ArgsType`, `@InputType`, `@Mutation`, `@Query`, `@Subscription`) produce the schema.\n- The **CRM object schema is built at runtime from metadata**: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/graphql/workspace-schema.factory.ts` calls `WorkspaceGraphqlSchemaSDLService.getOrComputeSchemaSDL(...)` then `makeExecutableSchema` with auto-generated resolvers from `WorkspaceResolverFactory`. SDL is cached per workspace/metadata version.\n- `graphql:generate` is a **frontend** target, not server. `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/project.json` (lines 252-270):\n  ```json\n  \"graphql:generate\": {\n    \"executor\": \"nx:run-commands\",\n    \"defaultConfiguration\": \"data\",\n    \"options\": { \"cwd\": \"{projectRoot}\", \"command\": \"dotenv graphql-codegen -- --config={args.config}\" },\n    \"configurations\": { \"data\": { \"config\": \"codegen.cjs\" }, \"metadata\": { \"config\": \"codegen-metadata.cjs\" }, \"admin\": { \"config\": \"codegen-admin.cjs\" } }\n  }\n  ```\n  `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/codegen.cjs` introspects a **running** server:\n  ```js\n  schema: (process.env.REACT_APP_SERVER_BASE_URL ?? 'http://localhost:3000') + '/graphql',\n  generates: { './src/generated/graphql.ts': { plugins: ['typescript','typescript-operations','typed-document-node'], ... } }\n  ```\n  So after adding/changing a server resolver you must run a live server and regenerate the three configs (`data`, `metadata`, `admin`) — CI checks this (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/.github/workflows/ci-server.yaml` lines 209-214).\n\n**Custom DTO/resolver pattern for a chat module** (copy `search`):\n- `@ArgsType()` class with `@Field(() => String)`, `@Field(() => Int)`, class-validator decorators — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/dtos/search-args.ts`.\n- `@ObjectType()` connection/edge/pageInfo DTOs — `search-result-connection.dto.ts`, `search-result-edge.dto.ts`, `search-result-page-info.dto.ts`.\n- Resolver — `search.resolver.ts` (shown above), with `@CoreResolver()` + `@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, CustomPermissionGuard)` + `@UsePipes(ResolverValidationPipe)` + `@UseFilters(...)`.\n\nFor system enums, use `UUIDScalarType` / `ConnectionCursorScalarType` from `src/engine/api/graphql/workspace-schema-builder/graphql-types/scalars`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Realtime / subscriptions\n\n### GraphQL subscriptions (4 exist)\n```\nsrc/engine/metadata-modules/logic-function/logic-function.resolver.ts:231\nsrc/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-chat/resolvers/agent-chat-subscription.resolver.ts:40\nsrc/engine/subscriptions/event-stream.resolver.ts:55\nsrc/engine/core-modules/event-logs/event-logs-live.resolver.ts:55\n```\n\nThe closest chat precedent is `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-chat/resolvers/agent-chat-subscription.resolver.ts`:\n```ts\n@MetadataResolver()\n@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard)\n@UseInterceptors(AiGraphqlApiExceptionInterceptor)\nexport class AgentChatSubscriptionResolver {\n  constructor(\n    private readonly subscriptionService: SubscriptionService,\n    private readonly agentChatStreamingService: AgentChatStreamingService,\n    @InjectWorkspaceScopedRepository(AgentChatThreadEntity)\n    private readonly threadRepository: WorkspaceScopedRepository<AgentChatThreadEntity>,\n  ) {}\n\n  @Subscription(() => AgentChatEventDTO, {\n    filter: (payload, variables) => payload.onAgentChatEvent.threadId === variables.threadId,\n  })\n  @UseGuards(SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.AI))\n  async onAgentChatEvent(@Args('threadId', { type: () => UUIDScalarType }) threadId: string, ...) {\n    // authorize, then\n    const iterator = await this.subscriptionService.subscribeToAgentChat({ workspaceId, threadId });\n    return wrapAsyncIteratorWithLifecycle(iterator, { initialValue: keepalivePayload, onHeartbeat, heartbeatIntervalMs });\n  }\n}\n```\nNote: subscription resolvers MUST be singleton (not request/transient scoped) — enforced with an error log in `@nestjs/graphql`.\n\nSupporting infra:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/subscriptions/subscription.service.ts` (`subscribeToAgentChat`, `publishToAgentChat`, `publishToEventStream`)\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/subscriptions/event-stream.resolver.ts`\n- `WorkspaceEventBroadcaster` — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/subscriptions/workspace-event-broadcaster/workspace-event-broadcaster.service.ts`\n\n### Realtime gateway (WebSocket/Redis, not GraphQL)\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/realtime-gateway/` — `services/realtime-gateway.service.ts`, `realtime-publisher.service.ts`, `presence.service.ts`, `realtime-topic-authorization.service.ts`.\n\nTopic grammar is already chat-aware (`.../utils/parse-realtime-topic.util.ts`):\n```ts\n// Topics: workspace:<id>[:kind:scope...]\nswitch (kind) {\n  case 'presence': return { kind: 'presence', workspaceId };\n  case 'chat':     return { kind: 'workspace', workspaceId, channelId: rest[0] };\n  case 'inbox':    return { kind: 'inbox', workspaceId, userId: rest[0] };\n  case 'object':   return { kind: 'object', workspaceId, objectNameSingular, recordId };\n}\n```\nACL today (`realtime-topic-authorization.service.ts`): workspace match always; inbox is user-scoped; **chat channel ACLs are not yet enforced** (only workspace membership). Per `docs/plan/03-integration-blueprint.md` §4, chat/presence topics target `workspace:<id>:chat:<channelId>` / `workspace:<id>:presence`. Note the `prd.json` deferred item: \"bullet-3 record/channel ACLs (P0.3 scope decision defers until object:/chat: publishers exist)\".\n\n---\n\n## 7. Base entity classes and `id` / uuid columns\n\n### For workspace entities\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/twenty-orm/base.workspace-entity.ts`:\n```ts\nexport abstract class BaseWorkspaceEntity {\n  id: string;\n  createdAt: string;\n  updatedAt: string;\n  deletedAt: string | null;\n}\n```\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/twenty-orm/custom.workspace-entity.ts` — `CustomWorkspaceEntity extends BaseWorkspaceEntity` (used by polymorphic target objects).\n\nThere is **no uuid decorator** here; `id` is a plain property. The `id` column is created from field metadata (`FieldMetadataType.UUID`, `defaultValue: 'uuid'`, see `compute-note-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts` lines 29-49).\n\n`EntityRelation<T>` is just `type EntityRelation<T> = T` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/workspace-migration/types/entity-relation.interface.ts`), used to dodge circular-import reflection.\n\n### For core TypeORM entities\n- `WorkspaceRelatedEntity` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/types/workspace-related-entity.ts`) — adds `workspaceId` + `workspace`.\n- `SyncableEntity extends WorkspaceRelatedEntity` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/types/syncable-entity.interface.ts`) — adds `universalIdentifier` + `applicationId`, with `@Index(['workspaceId','universalIdentifier'], { unique: true })`.\n\nUUID id column pattern (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/api-key/api-key.entity.ts`):\n```ts\n@Index('IDX_API_KEY_WORKSPACE_ID', ['workspaceId'])\n@Entity({ name: 'apiKey', schema: 'core' })\n@ObjectType('ApiKey')\nexport class ApiKeyEntity extends WorkspaceRelatedEntity {\n  @Field(() => UUIDScalarType)\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')\n  id: string;\n  ...\n  @Field(() => Date)\n  @CreateDateColumn({ type: 'timestamptz' })\n  createdAt: Date;\n\n  @Field(() => Date)\n  @UpdateDateColumn({ type: 'timestamptz' })\n  updatedAt: Date;\n}\n```\n`UUIDScalarType` import path: `src/engine/api/graphql/workspace-schema-builder/graphql-types/scalars`.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Soft delete\n\n### Workspace entities\n- `BaseWorkspaceEntity.deletedAt: string | null` is the only declaration.\n- The actual column exists only if the `deletedAt` **field metadata** is declared (system field; e.g. `compute-note-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts` lines 105-132). `buildWorkspaceTableShape` computes `hasDeletedAtColumn` (line 126).\n- API: `WorkspaceRepository.softDelete(criteria)` / `restore(criteria)` (lines 649/663 of `workspace-repository.ts`), used in the note hook service above.\n\n### Core entities\nTwo patterns:\n- `@DeleteDateColumn({ type: 'timestamptz' })` — e.g. `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/webhook/entities/webhook.entity.ts` lines 40-41.\n- Plain nullable column + repository `softDelete` — e.g. `AgentChatThreadEntity` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-chat/entities/agent-chat-thread.entity.ts`) uses `@Column({ type: 'timestamptz', nullable: true }) deletedAt: Date | null;` plus an index `@Index('IDX_AGENT_CHAT_THREAD_ID_DELETED_AT', ['id','deletedAt'])`, because `WorkspaceScopedRepository` manages soft-delete via criteria rather than TypeORM's `@DeleteDateColumn` semantics.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Cursor pagination\n\n### Auto-generated object `findMany` (metadata CRUD)\nArgs interface `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/graphql/workspace-resolver-builder/interfaces/workspace-resolvers-builder.interface.ts` (lines 27-30):\n```ts\nfirst?: number;\nlast?: number;\nbefore?: string;\nafter?: string;\n```\nPlus `filter`, `orderBy`. Response is a Relay-style connection with `edges { node, cursor }` and `pageInfo`.\n\nUtilities:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/api/graphql/graphql-query-runner/utils/cursors.util.ts` — `encodeCursor({ objectRecord, order, flatObjectMetadata, flatFieldMetadataMaps, orderByValuesFromScan })`, `decodeCursor(cursor)` (base64 JSON), `getCursor(args)` (reads `after`/`before`)