        "prompt": "I'm working in the A2E Suite monorepo (a Twenty CRM fork) at /Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite. I need to understand the exact conventions for adding a new server domain module under `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/<name>/` so I can create a `chat` module.\n\nPlease research and report back with concrete file paths, code excerpts, and structure. Be very thorough.\n\nSpecifically:\n1. Look at `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/modules.module.ts` and report exactly how modules are registered/imported.\n2. Pick the simplest existing domain module (e.g. `note` or `task`) and give its full file tree and the contents (or key parts) of:\n   - the `<name>.module.ts`\n   - an entity file (how `@ObjectType`, `@Entity`, `@Column`, `@Field` are used; base entity class; id generation; workspace scoping with `workspaceId`; soft-delete columns)\n   - a GraphQL resolver (decorators used: `@Resolver`, `@Query`, `@Mutation`, `@Args`, guards, pagination), how cursor pagination is done (is there a shared pagination util/type? `cursor`/`first`/`after` args?)\n   - a service\n3. Report how workspace scoping is enforced (workspaceId column, `@AuthWorkspace()`, guards) with a concrete example.\n4. Report how entities get registered with TypeORM (auto-loading globs? `TypeOrmModule.forFeature`? entity metadata modules?).\n5. Report how GraphQL schema files are organized and whether there is a required `*.graphql` file, and how `graphql:generate` works.\n6. Check whether any realtime/subscription GraphQL patterns exist (e.g. `@Subscription`) and where.\n7. Report the exact base entity classes available (e.g. `BaseWorkspaceEntity`, `BaseEntity`) and their import paths, and how `id` uuid columns are defined.\n8. Report how soft-delete is represented (`deletedAt` column) and whether there's a `@DeleteDateColumn` pattern.\n\nReturn a detailed structured report with file paths and code snippets. Do not modify any files.",
